    ('Bar and Lounge Neon', 'Scout for dimly-lit bar entrances with neon signs glowing in the windows, often featuring martini glasses, cocktails, or the bar''s name.', 'Locate neon sign reading ''BAR'', ''LOUNGE'', or bar name in glowing tubes, mounted on bar establishment exterior or window.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Neon''s inability to produce true black meant bar signs had to contrast against dark painted wood or mirrors rather than dark glass to be visible.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/711e988b5d04c75d.jpg', 2),
    ('Hotel Neon Signage', 'Look for vintage hotel buildings with large neon signs displayed on their roofline or facade, often from mid-20th century establishments.', 'Find illuminated neon spelling ''HOTEL'' or hotel name in bright neon colors, visible on hotel building entrance or marquee.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Hotel neon signs were often the tallest structures in small towns before the 1950s, serving as de facto landmarks for traveling salesmen and night drivers.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/687f4ed07ad9b50d.png', 3),
